lling, outside spending on either side, or a shift in the national House environment could move this toward a closer contest.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Stephanie Bice seeks a third term in a central Oklahoma district that leans Republican by about nine points. She has raised $2.4 million and holds a large cash advantage over Democrat Jena Nelson, a former teacher who won her primary and has drawn attention from national Democrats, who added the seat to their target list. Bice has so far declined to debate.\n\nNearly all expert raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, with a few calling it Likely Republican. A Democratic-sponsored September poll showed Bice ahead by five points, and prediction markets price her win probability near 88 percent. The evidence points to a Republican hold, though the district's history of close races and Democratic investment keep the door slightly ajar.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.099, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1151, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0881, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0678, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0911, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.097, "margin": -8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0816, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0827, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_d